# State Management Standards

## The Rule

`useState` is only allowed for **local UI toggles** that no other component needs.
Everything else lives in a Zustand store.

```tsx
// ✅ useState IS allowed for:
const [isExpanded, setIsExpanded] = useState(false)   // local accordion
const [hovering, setHovering] = useState(false)        // animation state
const [inputValue, setInputValue] = useState('')        // uncontrolled input (if not shared)

// ❌ useState is NOT allowed for:
const [userRole, setUserRole] = useState(null)          // → useAuthStore
const [showModal, setShowModal] = useState(false)       // if triggered from another component → store
const [resumes, setResumes] = useState([])              // any data fetched from API → store
const [currentPage, setCurrentPage] = useState('hub')  // navigation → useUIStore
const [installedBlocks, setInstalledBlocks] = useState([]) // hub data → useHubBlocksStore
```

## page.tsx Is Routing Only

`src/app/page.tsx` must contain **zero business logic and zero `useState` calls** (except the hydration `mounted` guard). All logic belongs in stores or shell components.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — logic in page.tsx
const [showProfileSetup, setShowProfileSetup] = useState(false)
useEffect(() => { /* profile check API call */ }, [userRole])

// ✅ GOOD — in useAuthStore
checkAndShowProfileSetup(walletAddress, userRole)
```

## Adding State to a Store

When adding new feature state, add it to the **relevant existing store** rather than creating a new store unless the feature is genuinely standalone:

| What | Store |
|---|---|
| Auth, role, profile setup | `useAuthStore` |
| Page navigation, modals, tabs | `useUIStore` |
| Installed hub blocks, picker open | `useHubBlocksStore` |
| DOT form data, step progress | `useDotApplicationStore` |
| Driver hub data (resumes, MVR, etc.) | `useDriverHubStore` (to be decomposed) |
| User preferences (persisted) | `usePreferencesStore` |

New blocks get their own store (e.g. `useMvrBlockStore`, `useResumeBlockStore`).
